                    "details": "- Shifts the current matrix by `(x, y, z)` (z defaults to 0 for the 2-argument form); everything drawn after this call is offset by that amount, until the matrix is restored by `popMatrix()`, `resetMatrix()`, or another `translate()`.\n- Units are the same logical pixels (or world units in 3D) as `drawRect` and the other drawing functions; see `drawRect` for the coordinate basics.\n- Order matters when combined with `rotate()` / `scale()`: `translate()` then `rotate()` rotates around the translated point; doing it the other way around rotates around the original origin and then moves along the rotated axes.\n- Usually wrapped in a `pushMatrix()` / `popMatrix()` pair so the offset does not leak into drawing that follows.",
