                    "desc": "Broadcast data to all clients and wait for every one of them (blocking)",
                    "details": "Queues the payload for every client first and then waits, so a slow peer no longer delays the clients behind it — but the call still returns only once all of them have it. Use broadcastAsync() to return immediately instead, and setSendTimeout() to bound the wait on unreliable peers.",
