                    "desc": "Queue data for every client and return at once; returns how many accepted it",
                    "details": "The payload is buffered once and shared by every client's queue, not copied per peer, so broadcasting a frame to twenty clients costs one copy. Clients whose queue is already at its high-water mark are skipped, which is why the return value can be less than getClientCount(). Each client that did accept it reports through onSendComplete.",
